    "source_clause": "Annex III",
    "frozen_requirement_text": "1. The upper edge of the warning triangle must be located vertically above the \"ICE\" mark, 1,000 mm higher than the Summer Load Line in fresh water but in no case higher than the deck line. The sides of the triangle must be 300 mm in length. 2. The ice class draught mark must be located 540 mm abaft of the centre of the load line ring or 540 mm abaft of the vertical line of the timber load line mark, if applicable. 3. The marks and figures must be cut out of 5 - 8 mm plate and then welded to the ship's side. The marks and figures must be painted in a red or yellow reflecting colour in order to make the marks and figures plainly visible, even in ice conditions. 4. The dimensions of all letters must be the same as those used in the load line mark.",
